                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "We Were Here Too somehow manages to turn a great co-op puzzle concept into an absolutely miserable experience.\r\n\r\nThe controls are fucking atrocious. Rotating objects and interacting with things feels like you're fighting the game itself. The puzzles are often confusing rather than clever, and the ridiculous time limits only make everything worse.\r\n\r\nAnd then there's THE FUCKING MAZE.\r\n\r\nSeriously, who designed this thing? Running around like an idiot against an absurdly tight timer while your friend desperately tries to guide you is not a clever puzzle. It's just frustrating bullshit.\r\n\r\nThat's where we finally gave up and uninstalled the game. We wanted to have a fun evening solving puzzles together, not develop anger management issues.\r\n\r\nI sincerely hope whoever designed that maze has to run through it every single time they need to take a shit.\r\n\r\nGreat concept, absolutely terrible execution. Not recommended.",
